From f18ac68936723d3660ac1ac46cfe2e32c1fa7e1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:59:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(desktop): work authority tracks effective
 runtime roles and same-ID routes, indexes drafts once

Review of d11f25f519 (REQUEST_CHANGES) found three defects in the work-source
authority observer:

1. P1 runtime-role ABA: the runtime index tracked the union of mirror/tile/main
   runtime IDs, so rebinding a tile or the main pane between runtimes that
   already had mirrors changed nothing; a cached all-five proof stayed valid and
   the idle stripe stayed done. The index now records each runtime's effective
   roles (mirror, tile, main) per qualified scope; any role change (including
   rt-a -> rt-b -> rt-a) bumps only the runtime epoch, revoking cached and
   in-flight runtime proof while durable proof is untouched.
2. P2 same-ID routes: the candidate index kept only the first row per bare ID, so
   a row for the same stored ID on another connection/profile starved the second
   legitimate owner of authority. The index keeps every row per alias in list
   order and each tracked scope resolves the candidate that names its own
   connection/profile, falling back to the first candidate (existing precedence,
   fail-closed). Exact-id rows still outrank lineage aliases.
3. P2 draft index cost: ownerLookupSessionRows() built a fresh recents+unshadowed
   draft array on every call, defeating the identity-keyed index (1000 rows /
   1000 mirrors: structural median ~180-220 ms with one draft vs ~4-7 ms
   without). withUnlistedOwnerStubs now memoizes on (rows, stubs) identity.

Proof: the three review repro tests are RED on d11f25f519 and GREEN here, with new
ABA / in-flight / unaffected-durable / main-pane tests, a three-route identical-ID
real HermesGateway registry test (both list orders, close + real reconnect +
fresh-read recovery), and an index-build counter test (kills the memo: 40600 vs
40400 rebuild count). Draft benchmark structural median 3.8 ms with and without
a draft; stream updates stay neutral.
